# Packed-list hostile ingress (#671), run by the OM-2 conductor (seed/qualification/om2/gate.om).
# Each fixture is first proven byte-identical to packet-corpus.om for its mode; then the compiled
# consumer pkt-consumer.om passes the fixture bytes from stdin to execprog. Expected exits come from
# the packed-list rules in OMEGESE.md: 0 or the exec'd program's output for a valid packet, trap 3
# (exit 103) for every malformed one. The trunc rows pass only the first K bytes of the 27-byte echo
# packet; every prefix shorter than 27 lacks a whole record and must be refused.
gen00-valid-one run seed/qualification/security673/packet-corpus.om rep:0:1 file:seed/qualification/security673/packets/p00.bin - 0
gen01-count-zero run seed/qualification/security673/packet-corpus.om rep:1:1 file:seed/qualification/security673/packets/p01.bin - 0
